     Cell[TextData[{"Flat portions mean the best exact-match count stays \
unchanged; a drop of 0.125 means one additional training term matches. \
A028552's final drop adds six matches at once. Only generation boundaries \
were recorded, so the connecting lines do not show every candidate or \
identify which operator caused an improvement."}], "Text"], 
     Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["Lower training loss is not yet evidence of \
discovering the sequence rule.", FontWeight -> Bold], " A002837 has zero \
training loss but fails at its 42nd recorded term. Of all 9,110 training \
fits, only 897 pass the next twelve terms and 91 match every recorded term. \
On the matched 2,048-entry control, evolution and evolution without mutation \
each achieve eight primary successes, versus nine for random search. Thus \
these curves show training progress and some predictive programs, but do not \
yet demonstrate a generalization advantage from mutation. Held-out terms were \
checked only for final selected programs, so there is no measured test-loss \
curve over generations."}], "Text"]}, Open]], 
